{"id":"8417c10a-71c2-4f21-a3fc-c3426adfd80a","object":"chat.completion","created":1785034462,"model":"deepseek-v4-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"{\n  \"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    if 'edges' not in case or 'refinement' not in case:\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"Missing required fields\\\")\\n    edges = case['edges']\\n    refinement = case['refinement']\\n    \\n    # Build member lists\\n    members = {}\\n    for node, group in refinement.items():\\n        members.setdefault(group, []).append(node)\\n    for group in members:\\n        members[group].sort()\\n    \\n    # Aggregate edges\\n    edge_weights = {}\\n    for edge in edges:\\n        if len(edge) != 3:\\n            raise ValueError(\\\"Invalid edge\\\")\\n        u, v, w = edge\\n        if u not in refinement or v not in refinement:\\n            raise ValueError(\\\"Edge node not in refinement\\\")\\n        gu = refinement[u]\\n        gv = refinement[v]\\n        if gu <= gv:\\n            key = (gu, gv)\\n        else:\\n            key = (gv, gu)\\n        edge_weights[key] = edge_weights.get(key, 0) + w\\n    \\n    aggregate_edges = [[k[0], k[1], v] for k, v in edge_weights.items()]\\n    aggregate_edges.sort(key=lambda x: (x[0], x[1]))\\n    \\n    return {\\n        'aggregate_edges': aggregate_edges,\\n        'members': members\\n    }\"\n}","reasoning_content":"We need to implement solve(case) for task DATA-LEI-02. The input payload has edges (list of [source, target, weight]) and refinement (mapping from node to group). The output must have \"aggregate_edges\" and \"members\". According to schema: aggregate_edges is an array of arrays of exactly 3 items: [string, string, number]. members is an object with dynamic keys from case.refinement.values() (so the group names). For each group, the value is an array of strings (the nodes in that group). The output must be deterministic. We need to map each node to its group, then for each edge, map endpoints to groups, then canonically order the pair (sorting? The schema says prefixItems, but it doesn't specify order. Usually undirected edges: we should sort the two group names lexicographically to avoid duplicates. Then sum weights for each pair (including self loops if both endpoints same group). Then sort aggregate_edges? The candidate text says \"Return sorted aggregate edges\". But schema doesn't require sorting; but output must be consistent. I'll sort by (group1, group2) lexicographically. For members, we need to list nodes in each group, sorted? The schema says items type string, no sort requirement but likely sorted for determinism. Use sorted node names. Note: payload may have _case_nonce, ignore. No mutation.\n\nImplementation: solve(case) - case is dict with keys edges, refinement, etc. Extract edges, refinement. Build groups dict: group -> list of nodes. For each node in refinement keys, add to group. Then build aggregate edges dict: key (sorted tuple of two group names) -> weight sum. For each edge [u, v, w], get gu, gv = refinement[u], refinement[v]. Sort pair (gu, gv) lexicographically (or use tuple sorted). Add w to that key. After processing all edges, convert aggregate_edges to list of [group1, group2, totalWeight]. Sort by group1 then group2. For members: sort list of nodes for each group. Return dict with aggregate_edges and members.\n\nCheck required fields: must have edges and refinement. If not, raise ValueError.\n\nNo randomness, no external calls.\n\nNow produce JSON with single key \"implementation\" containing Python source string.\n\nNeed to escape newlines and quotes properly.\n\nLet's write the Python code:\n\ndef solve(case):\n    # validate\n    if 'edges' not in case or 'refinement' not in case:\n        raise ValueError(\"Missing required fields\")\n    edges = case['edges']\n    refinement = case['refinement']\n    # Build groups\n    members_dict = {}\n    for node, group in refinement.items():\n        members_dict.setdefault(group, []).append(node)\n    # Sort each group's nodes\n    for group in members_dict:\n        members_dict[group].sort()\n    # Build aggregate edges\n    edge_weights = {}\n    for edge in edges:\n        if len(edge) != 3:\n            raise ValueError(\"Invalid edge\")\n        u, v, w = edge\n        if u not in refinement or v not in refinement:\n            raise ValueError(\"Edge node not in refinement\")\n        gu = refinement[u]\n        gv = refinement[v]\n        # canonical order\n        if gu <= gv:\n            key = (gu, gv)\n        else:\n            key = (gv, gu)\n        edge_weights[key] = edge_weights.get(key, 0) + w\n    # Convert to list of [group1, group2, weight]\n    aggregate_edges = [[k[0], k[1], v] for k, v in edge_weights.items()]\n    # Sort\n    aggregate_edges.sort(key=lambda x: (x[0], x[1]))\n    return {\n        \"aggregate_edges\": aggregate_edges,\n        \"members\": members_dict\n    }\n\nBut note: dynamicKeysFrom: case.refinement.values() - meaning the keys of members object should be exactly the values that appear in refinement (group names). We must ensure that we include all groups, even if they have no nodes? Actually refinement maps each node to a group, so each group that appears will have at least one node. So fine.\n\nAlso ensure that aggregate_edges list of arrays is correctly typed: numbers should be ints (or floats?), schema says number, so int is fine.\n\nNow write the final JSON."},"logprobs":null,"finish_reason":"stop"}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":1597,"completion_tokens":1278,"total_tokens":2875,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":1536},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":937},"prompt_cache_hit_tokens":1536,"prompt_cache_miss_tokens":61},"system_fingerprint":"fp_8b330d02d0_prod0820_fp8_kvcache_20260402"}